-- Test Description
-- The purpose of this test is to ensure the proper functionality of the GEM when 
-- transmitting frames and receiving pause frames at the same time.																																																																			   tion.
--
-- Test Coverage
-- � Ensures that the GEM works properly when the transmission a frame is currently 
--   halted and the pause frame counter is  non-zero.  Once the pause frame counter 
--   is zero, the GEM should correctly transmit the frame. (Transmitted frame should 
--   be identical to the frame that is buffered)
-- � Ensures that the GEM works properly when a frame is currently being transmitted 
--   and a pause frame is received.  However, the pause functionality in the GEM is 
--   not enabled.  (Therefore, the pause frame should not affect the transmission 
--   of the current frame)
-- � Ensures that if a frame is currently being transmitted and a pause frame 
--   is received with a non-zero pause time value that the pause counter does 
--   not begin counting until the current frame is finished transmitting.
-- � Ensures that if the pause counter is currently counting down and a new 
--   zero pause time frame is received that the GEM should resume transmissions 
--   immediately.
-- � Ensures that if the pause counter is currently counting down that the GEM 
--   should still able to transmit a pause frame.
--
-- Detailed Test Description
-- 1. Initialise the GEM for 100 mode operation.
-- 2. Enable receive and transmit.
-- 3. Enable the reception of pause frames.
-- 4. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches register 1, 
--    type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0x0008.  
--    Try to transmit a valid frame with valid CRC.  However, the frame should not 
--    be transmitted until the pause time counter is zero.  Once the pause 
--    time counter is zero the frame should be transmitted properly.
-- 5. Disable the reception of pause frames.
-- 6. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches pause 
--    frame address 0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 
--    and pause time to be set is 0x00FF.  Start transmitting a valid frame 
--    with crc.  The frame should be transmitted properly. 
--    (Since pause functionality is disabled,  GEM should transmit frame immediately)
-- 7. Re-enable pause frame functionality.
-- 8. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches pause 
--    frame address 0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 
--    and pause time to be set is 0x00FF.  The GEM should not halt 
--    transmission until the frame being transmitted in point 6 is finished.																																																			   ess.
-- 9. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches pause frame 
--    address 0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 #
--    and pause time to be set is 0x0020.  The pause time counter should 
--    start counting down.  However, another pause frame is received where 
--    the destination address matches pause frame address 0x0180C2000001, 
--    type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to 
--    be set is 0x0000.  Therefore, the GEM should be able to transmit
--    once the pause counter is equal to zero.  Try to transmit a valid
--    frame with crc to ensure that the GEM is able to transmit once the
--    zero pause frame is received.  (Frame should be transmitted successfully)
-- 10. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches pause
--     frame address 0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 
--     and pause time to be set is 0x00FF.  Transmit a pause frame where
--     the destination address matches pause frame address 0x0180C2000001,
--     type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set 
--     is 0x00FF.  (The GEM should be able to transmit pause frames even 
--     though the GEM cannot transmit normal frames because of the pause 
--     functionality)
-- 11. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure that the above
--     operations were handled properly.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

requires ext_fifo_interface 0
